{
  "$schema": "https://yamcs.org/schema/stack.schema.json",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "command",
      "name": "/ADCS/ADCS_ENABLE_CC",
      "extraOptions": [],
      "arguments": []
    },
    {
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/DEVICE_ENABLED",
          "operator": "eq",
          "value": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Let several device HK cycles (each carrying a GPS sample) land before certifying the clock: CFE_TIME_ToneSendGPS() accepts external data unconditionally while ClockSetState is NOT_SET (see cfe_time_tone.c), letting STCF settle before the tighter CFE_PLATFORM_TIME_MAX_DELTA acceptance window applies once the clock is marked valid below.",
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/DEVICE_COUNT",
          "operator": "gte",
          "value": "5"
        }
      ],
      "timeout": 30000
    },
    {
      "__comment": "A time SERVER's ClockSetState can only become WAS_SET via this ground command (see cfe_time_tone.c's CFE_TIME_ToneUpdate: the WAS_SET assignment is compiled only under CFE_PLATFORM_TIME_CFG_CLIENT, which is false here) -- it is the real, intended operational step where ground ops certifies a newly-live external time source. ADCS feeding CFE_TIME_ExternalGPS is only half of issue #8 item 5's chain; this is the other half.",
      "type": "command",
      "name": "/CFE_TIME/CFE_TIME_COMMANDS/CFE_TIME_SET_STATE",
      "extraOptions": [],
      "arguments": [
        {
          "name": "CLOCKSTATE",
          "value": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/CFE_TIME/CFE_TIME_HKPACKET/CLOCKSTATEAPI",
          "operator": "eq",
          "value": "0"
        }
      ],
      "timeout": 30000
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Confirms the clock isn't just VALID but actually anchored to the scenario's real calendar epoch (nominal-baseline's 2023-09-16T23:00:00Z), not some artifact epoch. SECONDSSTCF (STCF = AtToneSTCF = NewTime - CurrentMET, see cfe_time_tone.c/cfe_time_utils.c) approximates the GPS-derived absolute time, offset below it by whatever MET (cFE ES uptime, including boot settle before simulated t=0) has accrued by this step. Bounds are seconds-since-cFE-mission-epoch (1980-01-01) for 2023-09-16T23:00:00Z (1379372400), with a wide +/-1800s margin for that MET/run-timing variance -- still tight enough to catch a prior real bug where a broken 42-IPC time feed (elapsed/time-of-day seconds mistaken for an absolute epoch) put the clock near 1980 or 2000 instead (off by hundreds of millions of seconds).",
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/CFE_TIME/CFE_TIME_HKPACKET/SECONDSSTCF",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "1379370600"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/CFE_TIME/CFE_TIME_HKPACKET/SECONDSSTCF",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "1379374200"
        }
      ],
      "timeout": 5000
    }
  ],
  "advancement": {
    "acknowledgment": "Acknowledge_Sent",
    "wait": 1000
  }
}
